   "fen": "r3kb1r/p4ppp/2p1pnb1/q1ppN3/3P1BP1/2N1P2P/PPP2P2/R2Q1RK1 b kq - 2 11",
   "line": [
    "Ne5"
   ],
   "spoken": "That pawn thrust weakens the shelter in front of the king. The central knight jump looks intimidating but it's surface-level — it merely hits the loose pawn, which just needs careful defending, sidestepping the tempting queen move that runs into a knight fork."
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 310,
   "fen": "2r1kb1r/p4ppp/2p1pnb1/q1ppN3/3P1BP1/2N1P2P/PPP2P2/R2Q1RK1 w k - 3 12",
   "line": [
    "Rc8"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now a principle to bank — the rule of piece value: carry out any task with the least valuable piece that can do it. So a rook drops back to defend the pawn. It isn't glamorous, but pieces have to do the dirty work sometimes, and there's nothing wrong with that.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
